@startuml session_directory_enrichment
skinparam BackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam maxMessageSize 72
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
skinparam sequence {
    ArrowColor #0D47A1
    LifeLineBorderColor #1565C0
    LifeLineBackgroundColor #E3F2FD
    ParticipantBorderColor #1565C0
    ParticipantBackgroundColor #E3F2FD
    ParticipantFontColor #000000
    DatabaseBorderColor #2E7D32
    DatabaseBackgroundColor #E8F5E9
    DatabaseFontColor #000000
}
hide footbox

title Session Inventory and Enrichment — Source-Local Flow

participant "Directory Service" as Directory
participant "Environment Adapter" as Adapter
database "Native Session Store" as Native
database "Immutable Record Store" as Records
participant "Enrichment Scheduler" as Scheduler
participant "Sandboxed Worker" as Worker
participant "AX Mesh Anti-Entropy" as Mesh

autonumber

== Cheap inventory ==

Directory -> Adapter: inventory scan with prior cursor
Adapter -> Native: read allowlisted metadata and event tails
Native --> Adapter: native IDs, generations, bounded tail data
Adapter --> Directory: inventory observations + next cursor
Directory -> Directory: sanitize, validate, derive instance keys
Directory -> Records: publish immutable observation batch
Directory -> Scheduler: evaluate freshness for changed heads

== Enrichment ==

alt Current annotation matches exact head
    Scheduler --> Directory: no job required
else Missing or stale annotation
    Scheduler -> Adapter: request bounded public-history projection
    Adapter -> Native: read exact snapshot/head
    Native --> Adapter: public events or canonical references
    Adapter --> Scheduler: typed redacted input + evidence IDs
    Scheduler -> Worker: title/summary job without mutation tools
    Worker --> Scheduler: schema-validated annotation candidate
    Scheduler -> Scheduler: verify head, policy, size, and provenance
    alt Head changed during job
        Scheduler -> Records: retain superseded job receipt only
    else Head unchanged
        Scheduler -> Records: publish annotation and success receipt
    end
end

== Mesh visibility ==

Records -> Mesh: inventory/annotation IDs and allowed objects
Mesh --> Directory: peer records converge by anti-entropy
Directory -> Directory: rebuild global catalog and stale/offline state

@enduml
